# Code owners for NorthStar
#
# Every path in the repo is owned by @BModz. Combined with the branch protection rule on
# `main` (one approving review, code owner review required), this means no change reaches
# `main` without a review from @BModz. Teammates still push branches and open pull requests
# freely, and they merge their own pull request once it is approved.
#
# Why a single owner rather than the four workstream teams: the org is half populated (5 of
# 9 people), several teams have one member or none, and a code owner cannot approve their
# own pull request, so team ownership currently deadlocks more pull requests than it routes.
# A single owner also keeps one person accountable for the shared core while the schema is
# still moving.
#
# Rules are matched last to first, so the most specific rule that matches a file wins.
# Only the version of this file on the default branch has any effect.
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners

*                               @BModz

